       base  and  returns  a _n_e_t_e_n_t structure containing the broken‐out fields
       from the entry.  A connection is opened to the database if necessary.

       The ggeettnneettbbyynnaammee() function returns a _n_e_t_e_n_t structure  for  the  entry
       from the database that matches the network _n_a_m_e.

       The  ggeettnneettbbyyaaddddrr()  function  returns a _n_e_t_e_n_t structure for the entry
       from the database that matches the network number  _n_e_t  of  type  _t_y_p_e.
       The _n_e_t argument must be in host byte order.

       The  sseettnneetteenntt()  function opens a connection to the database, and sets
       the next entry to the first entry.  If _s_t_a_y_o_p_e_n is  nonzero,  then  the
       connection  to  the database will not be closed between calls to one of
